    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d451">

                <pb facs="0824" n="762" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg762"/>

                <head>No. 446.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hoffman to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-06-06"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 6,
                        1878</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 43.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to forward to you herewith
                    a copy of translation of a note from Mr. de Giers, in relation to injury done by
                    foreign <pb facs="0825" n="763" xml:id="pg763"/> vessels to the torpedoes in the
                    port of Odessa. Mr. de Giers requests that the dispositions taken by the
                    authorities of Odessa may be brought to the attention of our people.</p>
                <p>If I am correctly informed, although large quantities of the products of the
                    United States are imported into Odessa, they are brought almost exclusively in
                    foreign bottoms. Our flag is rarely seen in that port.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WICKHAM HOFFMAN.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d451-a1.xml" xpointer="d451-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
